==Usage== <!--T:26-->

<!--T:42-->
# Select a single sketch or one or more faces from the Body.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:PartDesign_Pad.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_Pad|Pad]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part Design → Additive Features → [[Image:PartDesign_Pad.svg|16px]] Pad}} option from the menu.
# Set the Pad parameters, see [[#Options|Options]] below.
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button.

==Options== <!--T:27-->

<!--T:43-->
When creating a pad, or after double-clicking an existing pad in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]], the '''Pad Parameters''' and '''Preview''' task panel is shown. It offers the following settings:

<!--T:28-->
[[Image:PartDesign_Pad_Taskpanel.png|frame|left]]

=== Start === <!--T:88-->

<!--T:89-->
Sets where the pad begins. By default the pad starts at the sketch or face used as its profile. {{Version|26.3}}
* '''Profile plane''' (default): the pad starts directly at the profile's sketch plane or face.
* '''Offset''': the pad starts at a numerical distance from the profile, entered in the '''Offset''' field.
* '''Reference''': the pad starts at a face, [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]], or sketch selected with the {{Button|Pick Reference}} button.

<!--T:90-->
This is useful to create multiple features from a single master sketch without needing separate offset planes for each one.

===Direction=== <!--T:93-->

<!--T:94-->
You can select how the pad is created:
* '''One sided''': the pad extends on one side of the face.
* '''Two sided''': the pad extends on both sides of the face. Two sub-menus (Side 1 and Side 2) appear to define the pad for each side.
* '''Symmetric''': the pad is symmetrical with respect to the original face.

===Type=== <!--T:29-->

<!--T:44-->
Type offers five different ways of specifying the length of the pad:

====Dimension==== <!--T:45-->

<!--T:46-->
Enter a numeric value for the '''Length''' of the pad. With the option '''Symmetric to plane''' the pad will extend half the given length to either side of the sketch or face.

====To last==== <!--T:49-->

<!--T:50-->
The pad will extend up to the last face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.

====To first==== <!--T:51-->

<!--T:52-->
The pad will extend up to the first face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.

====Up to face==== <!--T:53-->

<!--T:54-->
The pad will extend up to a face. Press the {{Button|Select face}} button and select a face or a [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]] from the Body.

====Up to shape==== <!--T:85-->

<!--T:86-->
{{Version|1.0}}: The pad will extend up to the selected shape. Optionally press the {{Button|Select shape}} button and select a shape. Leave the {{Button|Select all faces}} checkbox enabled or disable it, press the {{Button|Select faces}} button and select the faces up to which the pad should be created.

===Length=== <!--T:30-->

<!--T:55-->
Defines the length of the pad.

=== Taper angle === <!--T:69-->

<!--T:71-->
Tapers the pad in the extrusion direction by the given angle. A positive angle means the outer pad border gets wider.

=== Reversed === <!--T:32-->

<!--T:57-->
Reverses the direction of the pad.

===Direction=== <!--T:65-->

==== Direction/edge ==== <!--T:66-->

<!--T:67-->
You can select the direction of the extrusion:

<!--T:68-->
* '''Sketch normal''' or '''Face normal:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of its normal. If you have selected several sketches or faces to be extruded, the normal of the first one will be used.
* '''Select reference…:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of a straight edge or a [[Part_DatumLine|datum line]] selected from the Body.
* '''Custom direction:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of the specified vector.

